<title>FRANCE: French consumer spending down 1.1 pct in May.</title>
<headline>French consumer spending down 1.1 pct in May.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted figures for household spending on manufactured goods in billions of 1980 francs:</p>
<p>					    May    Apr    Mar     May 1996</p>
<p> Total				   57.85  58.49   57.82     57.62</p>
<p> Total change (pct v pvs month)   -1.1    1.2     0.2	-0.1</p>
<p> Retail sector			 39.28  39.42   38.43     37.64</p>
<p> Durables				16.92  17.37   16.77     17.54</p>
<p> Cars				     5.90   6.43    6.52	7.24</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		   11.22  11.53   11.35     10.79</p>
<p> Other				   29.72  29.59   29.70     29.29</p>
<p>It gave the following percentage changes (month-on-month unless stated)</p>
<p>					    May    Apr    March  May yr/yr</p>
<p> Total				   -1.1    1.2     0.2	  0.4</p>
<p> Retail sector			 -0.4    2.6    -0.3	  4.4</p>
<p> Durables				-2.6    3.6    -0.2	 -3.6</p>
<p>   of which cars		     -8.2   -1.3     1.4	-18.5</p>
<p>   household equip		    0.7    6.7    -1.2	  6.9</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		   -2.7    1.5     1.2	  4.0</p>
<p> Other				    0.4   -0.3     0.0	  1.5</p>
<p>INSEE originally said consumer spending rose 1.5 percent in April.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
